WEBVTT

00:15:59.329 --> 00:16:02.746
One of the pieces of research that
we put out last year that

00:16:02.746 --> 00:16:07.204
I was most proud of and most excited
about is what we call reinforcement

00:16:07.204 --> 00:16:08.537
learning from human feedback.

00:16:08.787 --> 00:16:11.621
And we showed that we can take these
giant models that are trained on

00:16:11.621 --> 00:16:14.329
a bunch of stuff, some of it good,
some of the bad,

00:16:14.662 --> 00:16:19.996
and then with a really quite small amount
of feedback from human judgment about,

00:16:19.996 --> 00:16:21.996
hey, this is good, this
is bad, this is wrong,

00:16:21.996 --> 00:16:24.287
this is the behavior I want I
don't want this behavior.

00:16:24.662 --> 00:16:29.662
We can feed that information from the
human judges back into the model

00:16:29.662 --> 00:16:32.954
and we can teach the model, behave more
like this and less like that.